        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): catch unhandled rejections in webhook and ingress worker shutdown",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Telegram webhook shutdown could leave owned resources active when an early teardown step failed: a synchronous `server.close()` throw, a `bot.stop()` rejection, or a transport-close rejection could skip later cleanup (bot stop, undici transport close, webhook status, diagnostic heartbeat). Ingress-worker `stop()` could also race on repeated calls and leave `worker.terminate()` rejections unobserved.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nIndependently guard each ordered webhook shutdown phase via `runTelegramWebhookShutdownPhases` so one sync/async failure cannot skip later owned cleanup, and wrap the path so fire-and-forget abort listeners never leak unhandled rejections. Startup failure cleanup uses `.catch(() => undefined)` so cleanup noise cannot mask the original startup error. Ingress-worker `stop()` shares one in-flight promise and observes terminate rejections.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators restarting or aborting a Telegram webhook account no longer risk leaked transports, stale webhook connected status, or leftover diagnostic heartbeats when one shutdown step fails. Process logs no longer see unhandled rejections from webhook/ingress shutdown paths.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `dc6452bf7ea4f208caf64f87c03019d1eeb86d2d`\n\n### Focused tests\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/webhook.test.ts -- --run -t \"does not leak unhandled|does not skip\"\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/webhook-shutdown.proof.test.ts -- --run\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/telegram/src/telegram-ingress-worker.test.ts -- --run\n```\n\nObserved: 4 webhook shutdown tests passed; proof test passed; 3 ingress-worker tests passed.\n\n### Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior addressed: sync `server.close()` throw must not skip bot/transport/status/diagnostics cleanup.\nReal environment tested: local Node production-path helper + negative nested-control-flow control (no live Telegram token required for this cleanup contract).\n\nExact commands run:\n\n```bash\nnode --import tsx extensions/telegram/src/proof-telegram-webhook-shutdown.mts\n```\n\nObserved output after fix:\n\n```text\nnode=v22.22.0\nhead=dc6452bf7ea4f208caf64f87c03019d1eeb86d2d\n\n[case 1] negative control — sync server.close throw skips later cleanup\n  ok: closeServer ran once\n  ok: stopBot was skipped\n  ok: closeTransport was skipped\n  ok: noteStop was skipped\n  ok: stopDiagnostics was skipped\n  ok: outer catch logged unexpected error\n  info: closeServer=1 stopBot=0 closeTransport=0 noteStop=0 stopDiagnostics=0 errors=1\n\n[case 2] positive control — sync server.close throw continues cleanup\n  ok: abort + drain + closeServer ran\n  ok: stopBot still ran\n  ok: closeTransport still ran\n  ok: noteStop still ran\n  ok: stopDiagnostics still ran\n  ok: server close failure was logged\n  ok: shutdown promise did not reject\n  info: stopBot=1 closeTransport=1 noteStop=1 stopDiagnostics=1 errors=[\"webhook server close failed: server close failed\"]\n\n[case 3] valid path — clean server.close runs full teardown\n  ok: every phase ran exactly once\n  ok: no errors logged on clean path\n  info: phases_ok=true errors=0\n\n=== Summary ===\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS: 15 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\nEvidence:\n- Negative control reproduces the pre-fix nested try/finally skip.\n- Positive control proves guarded phases continue after sync close throw.\n- Valid path proves clean close still runs full ordered teardown.\n- Vitest integration: `server.close` monkeypatch on a real started webhook still runs stop/transport/status/diagnostics with no unhandledRejection.\n\nWhat was not tested: live configured Telegram Bot API gateway restart with a real bot token (cleanup contract is local HTTP + owned transport teardown, not Bot API delivery).\n\nLOC: `extensions/telegram/src/webhook.ts` stays at baseline line count (helper extracted to `webhook-shutdown.ts`).\n",
        "branch": "fix/channel-bugs-batch-2026-07-06",
